.TH "DEDB LSGOG" "1" "2026-01-01" "0.1.0" "dedb lsgog Manual"
.SH NAME
dedb\-lsgog \- List owned GOG games and whether they look DOSBox-based, without downloading...
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dedb lsgog
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List owned GOG games and whether they look DOSBox-based, without downloading anything.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-1\fP
Just `gog:<id>` per line - no classification column.
.TP
\fB\-\-dos\fP / \-\-all
--dos (default): only DOSBox-based games. --all: every owned game.
.TP
\fB\-r,\fP \-\-refreshmetadata
Re-fetch GOG dependency metadata instead of using the cached copy.
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fP
Don't contact GOG at all - use only local files and cached metadata.
.TP
\fB\-v,\fP \-\-verbose
Print each network request to GOG as it happens.
